  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - PORTS OF CARTAGENA AND CONTECAR CENTRAL SECURITY &amp; CUSTOMS FACILITY, through Government of Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $400,000 feasibility study for the Sociedad Porturaria Regional de Cartagena S.A. (SPRC) develops a central customs and security facility to serve the SPRC Ports of Cartagena and Contecar. The project will supplement and expand container handling capacity at Cartagena and improve SPRC&apos;s competitive position. The feasibility study complements the USTDA-funded Cartagena Secure Port Initiative, and further expands the development of a conceptual plan and operating procedures for a central inspection station, including plans for the physical layout, security, network, and procedures and equipment for a regional database.</narrative>
  </description>
